LGFsD0vRHleU5fVLV_s1oRrWmSeHv2u7W0Pca9hilNHXscLg3IJenmJ709gb1KDIASJMdaJvMrq=
xtVAtg&_hsmi=3D397629232 ) services, while smaller ones like College Hunks =
Hauling Junk & Moving are looking to enter the business to handle heavier r=
eturn items following customer inquiries.

=E2=80=98Tis the season of returns

An estimated 17% of holiday purchases will be returned, and 82% (https://a-=
us.storyblok.com/f/1021220/x/6e22cae2b7/2025-retail-returns-landscape.pdf?_=
hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9J2Ld-ZTcf_LGFsD0vRHleU5fVLV_s1oRrWmSeHv2u7W0Pca9hilNHXscLg=
3IJenmJ709gb1KDIASJMdaJvMrqxtVAtg&_hsmi=3D397629232 ) of people will return=
 a holiday gift within a month of receiving it, per the National Retail Fed=
eration.

Historically, January and February are the biggest months for returns, duri=
ng which ReturnQueen expects to see a 15%-20% increase in demand.

But returns aren=E2=80=99t just a seasonal issue

Americans are estimated to have returned ~$850B worth of merchandise in 202=
5, and overall return rates have doubled (https://institute.bankofamerica.c=
om/economic-insights/retail-returns.html?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9J2Ld-ZTcf_LGFsD0=
vRHleU5fVLV_s1oRrWmSeHv2u7W0Pca9hilNHXscLg3IJenmJ709gb1KDIASJMdaJvMrqxtVAtg=
&_hsmi=3D397629232 ) since 2019.

And while returns can be a nuisance for consumers, for retailers, they can =
present huge operational costs. A 2023 report (https://www.optoro.com/retur=
ns-blog/optoro-impact-report-2023/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9J2Ld-ZTcf_LGFsD0vRHleU=
5fVLV_s1oRrWmSeHv2u7W0Pca9hilNHXscLg3IJenmJ709gb1KDIASJMdaJvMrqxtVAtg&_hsmi=
=3D397629232#:~:text=3DThe%20average%20return%20rate%20for,had%20a%20better=
%20return%20policy .) found that processing a return can cost retailers 30%=
 of the item=E2=80=99s original price, and many returns often end up in lan=
dfills (https://abcnews.go.com/Business/wireStory/holiday-gift-returns-land=
fill-128703533?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9J2Ld-ZTcf_LGFsD0vRHleU5fVLV_s1oRrWmSeHv2u7=
W0Pca9hilNHXscLg3IJenmJ709gb1KDIASJMdaJvMrqxtVAtg&_hsmi=3D397629232 ) .

To handle the growing number of returns, the NRF found that ~75% of retaile=
rs are now charging restocking fees =E2=80=94 some as high as $45 (https://=
nypost.com/2025/12/25/lifestyle/retail-stores-now-charge-customers-eye-wate=
ring-return-fees/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9J2Ld-ZTcf_LGFsD0vRHleU5fVLV_s1oRrWmSeHv=
2u7W0Pca9hilNHXscLg3IJenmJ709gb1KDIASJMdaJvMrqxtVAtg&_hsmi=3D397629232 ) .

Tack the cost of a return service onto those restocking fees, and it might =
just be worth it to keep pretending to love that sweater until you actually=
 do.

